  "id": "nonlinear-transformation",
  "term": "nonlinear transformation",
  "definition": "In this psychology context, nonlinear transformation refers to a change process in which factors such as passion, self-efficacy, and emotional resources influence outcomes like job satisfaction in a non-straight-line way. Small differences can produce much larger or threshold-based changes, especially at critical transition points.",
